KOSH INNOVATIONS GLOBAL ITEM CREATION PORTAL
COMMUNICATION & NOTIFICATION HUB — DETAILED IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT
Email + WhatsApp + Templates + Broadcasts + Notification Centre + Delivery Queue + Status & Audit
Version: 1.0
Purpose: Add a complete, configurable Communication & Notification Hub to the existing application without removing, shrinking, or breaking any existing functionality.

====================================================================
1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE AND NON-NEGOTIABLE REQUIREMENTS
====================================================================

Implement a unified Communication & Notification Hub for the existing Kosh Innovations Global IT / Global Item Creation Portal. The Hub must centrally coordinate application notifications and delivery workflows while providing separate, dedicated configuration pages for Email and WhatsApp.

The application must provide, at minimum, these separate pages:
1. Communication & Notification Hub — overview and operational dashboard.
2. Email Configuration — email provider, sender identity, connection settings, test, activation and health.
3. WhatsApp Configuration — WhatsApp mode, official API/provider settings, sender/business identity, webhook, test and health.
4. Email Template Management — create, edit, preview, test, version, approve, activate and retire templates.
5. WhatsApp Template Management — create and manage approved WhatsApp templates where required by the chosen provider; support user-assisted message drafts separately.
6. Broadcast Campaigns — draft, validate, approve, schedule, pause, resume, cancel and review email/WhatsApp campaigns.
7. Notification Rules & Event Mapping — decide which application events generate notifications, which channels are eligible, who receives them, and under which conditions.
8. Notification Centre / Inbox — in-application notifications, read/unread state, filters, search, deep links and acknowledgement where appropriate.
9. Delivery Queue — durable queued messages with channel, priority, scheduled time, attempts, next retry, lease/worker state and cancellation where permitted.
10. Delivery Status & Message Tracking — per-recipient, per-channel lifecycle and provider receipts, with accurate distinctions between queued, sent, accepted, delivered, read, failed and unknown.
11. Failed Deliveries & Retry Management — inspect failures, correct configuration, retry safely, suppress unsafe retries and replay eligible jobs.
12. Delivery Logs & Audit Trail — searchable operational events and immutable or append-only audit records for administrative actions.
13. Provider Webhooks & Events — secure inbound status events, validation, deduplication and processing history.
14. Communication Preferences & Consent — recipient preferences, channel eligibility, consent/opt-out, suppression and policy checks.
15. Communication Reports — operational and campaign reports based on verified event data.
16. Configuration Versions & Change History — versioned settings, template changes, campaign changes, rules and approvals.

Use the existing application's navigation, authorization, design system, database conventions, API conventions and approval workflow. Do not create an unrelated standalone application unless the existing architecture explicitly requires a separate service. Integrate the Hub into the existing application as a cohesive module.

IMPORTANT: Email and WhatsApp must have separate configuration pages and separate template-management pages. They must still be orchestrated by one common Notification Hub, event/rule engine, queueing model, delivery tracking layer, audit trail and reporting layer. A common hub does not mean that the channel-specific settings are merged into one confusing form.

Do not remove, rename, simplify, or overwrite any existing requirements, pages, item master functionality, SAP Business One integration, governance, dashboard or approval workflow. This prompt adds a module to the existing product.

