14. DELIVERY STATUS, RECEIPTS AND MESSAGE LIFECYCLE
====================================================================

Track message status separately from campaign status, notification intent status and queue worker status.

For each outbound message, maintain an append-only lifecycle/event history:
- Event ID.
- Message ID.
- Channel.
- Previous and new internal status.
- Original provider status/event type, if any.
- Provider message ID, if available.
- Source: application, queue worker, provider API response, verified webhook, reconciliation process or human operator.
- Event timestamp and received timestamp.
- Correlation ID.
- Safe error code/category.
- Actor/service identity.
- Relevant configuration/template version identifiers.

Rules:
- API request success may mean only that a request was accepted. Map it only to the state supported by the provider's response.
- Delivered status requires a trustworthy delivery receipt or provider event.
- Read status is only available where the provider actually supplies it and must not be inferred.
- Webhook events may arrive late, out of order or more than once. Deduplicate and process idempotently.
- Store raw webhook payloads only when necessary, protected and for a limited retention period. Prefer a redacted/minimized payload plus a payload hash and event metadata.
- Preserve the original provider status even when mapped to an internal status.
- Handle status regressions and out-of-order events through an explicit state-transition policy. Do not overwrite a later verified state with an older event.
- Distinguish user-reported outcomes in USER_ASSISTED WhatsApp mode from provider-confirmed outcomes.
- Expose uncertainty honestly. If the provider offers no delivery status, say so in the UI.

