24. PERFORMANCE, SCALING AND RESILIENCE
====================================================================

- Use asynchronous workers for external delivery.
- Keep business request latency independent from provider response latency.
- Apply configurable concurrency and provider-specific rate limits.
- Use bounded queues and alert on backlogs.
- Use database transactions and idempotency protections.
- Implement safe graceful shutdown and worker lease recovery.
- Use exponential backoff with jitter where appropriate.
- Avoid retry storms after a provider outage.
- Support per-provider circuit breaking or equivalent outage protection if suitable for the existing stack.
- Ensure one failing channel does not block another channel or in-app notification processing.
- Support pagination and server-side filtering for large delivery logs.
- Archive or purge records according to an approved retention policy.
- Add database indexes based on measured query patterns.
- Avoid logging entire message bodies or provider payloads by default.
- Test concurrency, worker restarts, duplicate requests, out-of-order webhooks and provider outages.

